---@field filter? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2DiscoveryBigQueryFilter Required. The tables the discovery cadence applies to. The first target with a matching filter will be the one to apply to a table.
---@field disabled? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2Disabled Tables that match this filter will not have profiles created.
---@field conditions? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2DiscoveryBigQueryConditions In addition to matching the filter, these conditions must be true before a profile is generated.
---@field cadence? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2DiscoveryGenerationCadence How often and when to update profiles. New tables that match both the filter and conditions are scanned as quickly as possible depending on system capacity.

---Message defining a field of a BigQuery table.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BigQueryField
---@field table? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BigQueryTable Source table of the field.
---@field field? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2FieldId Designated field in the BigQuery table.

---Row key for identifying a record in BigQuery table.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BigQueryKey
---@field rowNumber? string Row number inferred at the time the table was scanned. This value is nondeterministic, cannot be queried, and may be null for inspection jobs. To locate findings within a table, specify `inspect_job.storage_config.big_query_options.identifying_fields` in `CreateDlpJobRequest`.
---@field tableReference? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BigQueryTable Complete BigQuery table reference.

---Options defining BigQuery table and row identifiers.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BigQueryOptions
---@field identifyingFields? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2FieldIdList Table fields that may uniquely identify a row within the table. When `actions.saveFindings.outputConfig.table` is specified, the values of columns specified here are available in the output table under `location.content_locations.record_location.record_key.id_values`. Nested fields such as `person.birthdate.year` are allowed.
---@field tableReference? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BigQueryTable Complete BigQuery table reference.
---@field excludedFields? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2FieldIdList References to fields excluded from scanning. This allows you to skip inspection of entire columns which you know have no findings. When inspecting a table, we recommend that you inspect all columns. Otherwise, findings might be affected because hints from excluded columns will not be used.
---@field rowsLimitPercent? number Max percentage of rows to scan. The rest are omitted. The number of rows scanned is rounded down. Must be between 0 and 100, inclusively. Both 0 and 100 means no limit. Defaults to 0. Only one of rows_limit and rows_limit_percent can be specified. Cannot be used in conjunction with TimespanConfig. Caution: A [known issue](https://docs.cloud.google.com/sensitive-data-protection/docs/known-issues#bq-sampling) is causing the `rowsLimitPercent` field to behave unexpectedly. We recommend using `rowsLimit` instead.
---@field rowsLimit? string Max number of rows to scan. If the table has more rows than this value, the rest of the rows are omitted. If not set, or if set to 0, all rows will be scanned. Only one of rows_limit and rows_limit_percent can be specified. Cannot be used in conjunction with TimespanConfig.
---@field includedFields? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2FieldIdList Limit scanning only to these fields. When inspecting a table, we recommend that you inspect all columns. Otherwise, findings might be affected because hints from excluded columns will not be used.
---@field sampleMethod? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BigQueryOptionsSampleMethodEnum|string How to sample the data.

---@alias gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BigQueryOptionsSampleMethodEnum "SAMPLE_METHOD_UNSPECIFIED"|"TOP"|"RANDOM_START"

---A pattern to match against one or more tables, datasets, or projects that contain BigQuery tables. At least one pattern must be specified. Regular expressions use RE2 [syntax](https://github.com/google/re2/wiki/Syntax); a guide can be found under the google/re2 repository on GitHub.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BigQueryRegex
---@field datasetIdRegex? string If unset, this property matches all datasets.
---@field tableIdRegex? string If unset, this property matches all tables.
---@field projectIdRegex? string For organizations, if unset, will match all projects. Has no effect for data profile configurations created within a project.

---@alias gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BigQueryRegexList gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BigQueryRegex[]

---A collection of regular expressions to determine what tables to match against.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BigQueryRegexes
---@field patterns? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BigQueryRegexList A single BigQuery regular expression pattern to match against one or more tables, datasets, or projects that contain BigQuery tables.

---Message defining the location of a BigQuery table. A table is uniquely identified by its project_id, dataset_id, and table_name. Within a query a table is often referenced with a string in the format of: `:.` or `..`.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BigQueryTable
---@field projectId? string The Google Cloud project ID of the project containing the table. If omitted, project ID is inferred from the API call.
---@field datasetId? string Dataset ID of the table.
---@field tableId? string Name of the table.

---Specifies a collection of BigQuery tables. Used for Discovery.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BigQueryTableCollection
---@field includeRegexes? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BigQueryRegexes A collection of regular expressions to match a BigQuery table against.

---The types of BigQuery tables supported by Cloud DLP.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BigQueryTableTypes
---@field types? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BigQueryTableTypesTypesItemEnumList A set of BigQuery table types.

---@alias gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BigQueryTableTypesTypesItemEnum "BIG_QUERY_TABLE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"BIG_QUERY_TABLE_TYPE_TABLE"|"BIG_QUERY_TABLE_TYPE_EXTERNAL_BIG_LAKE"|"BIG_QUERY_TABLE_TYPE_SNAPSHOT"

---@alias gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BigQueryTableTypesTypesItemEnumList (gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BigQueryTableTypesTypesItemEnum|string)[]

---Bounding box encompassing detected text within an image. Coordinates are in pixels and strictly within the image or frame bounds.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BoundingBox
---@field height? number Height of the bounding box in pixels.
---@field width? number Width of the bounding box in pixels.
---@field top? number Top coordinate of the bounding box. (0,0) is upper left.
---@field left? number Left coordinate of the bounding box. (0,0) is upper left.

---@alias gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BoundingBoxList gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BoundingBox[]

---Bucket is represented as a range, along with replacement values.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2Bucket
---@field max? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2Value Upper bound of the range, exclusive; type must match min.
---@field replacementValue? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2Value Required. Replacement value for this bucket.
---@field min? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2Value Lower bound of the range, inclusive. Type should be the same as max if used.

---@alias gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BucketList gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2Bucket[]

---Generalization function that buckets values based on ranges. The ranges and replacement values are dynamically provided by the user for custom behavior, such as 1-30 -> LOW, 31-65 -> MEDIUM, 66-100 -> HIGH. This can be used on data of type: number, long, string, timestamp. If the bound `Value` type differs from the type of data being transformed, we will first attempt converting the type of the data to be transformed to match the type of the bound before comparing. See https://docs.cloud.google.com/sensitive-data-protection/docs/concepts-bucketing to learn more.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BucketingConfig
---@field buckets? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2BucketList Set of buckets. Ranges must be non-overlapping.

