---Compute numerical stats over an individual column, including number of distinct values and value count distribution.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CategoricalStatsConfig
---@field field? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2FieldId Field to compute categorical stats on. All column types are supported except for arrays and structs. However, it may be more informative to use NumericalStats when the field type is supported, depending on the data.

---Histogram of value frequencies in the column.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CategoricalStatsHistogramBucket
---@field valueFrequencyUpperBound? string Upper bound on the value frequency of the values in this bucket.
---@field bucketValueCount? string Total number of distinct values in this bucket.
---@field bucketSize? string Total number of values in this bucket.
---@field valueFrequencyLowerBound? string Lower bound on the value frequency of the values in this bucket.
---@field bucketValues? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2ValueFrequencyList Sample of value frequencies in this bucket. The total number of values returned per bucket is capped at 20.

---@alias gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CategoricalStatsHistogramBucketList gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CategoricalStatsHistogramBucket[]

---Result of the categorical stats computation.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CategoricalStatsResult
---@field valueFrequencyHistogramBuckets? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CategoricalStatsHistogramBucketList Histogram of value frequencies in the column.

---Partially mask a string by replacing a given number of characters with a fixed character. Masking can start from the beginning or end of the string. This can be used on data of any type (numbers, longs, and so on) and when de-identifying structured data we'll attempt to preserve the original data's type. (This allows you to take a long like 123 and modify it to a string like **3.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CharacterMaskConfig
---@field maskingCharacter? string Character to use to mask the sensitive values—for example, `*` for an alphabetic string such as a name, or `0` for a numeric string such as ZIP code or credit card number. This string must have a length of 1. If not supplied, this value defaults to `*` for strings, and `0` for digits.
---@field charactersToIgnore? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CharsToIgnoreList When masking a string, items in this list will be skipped when replacing characters. For example, if the input string is `555-555-5555` and you instruct Cloud DLP to skip `-` and mask 5 characters with `*`, Cloud DLP returns `***-**5-5555`.
---@field numberToMask? number Number of characters to mask. If not set, all matching chars will be masked. Skipped characters do not count towards this tally. If `number_to_mask` is negative, this denotes inverse masking. Cloud DLP masks all but a number of characters. For example, suppose you have the following values: - `masking_character` is `*` - `number_to_mask` is `-4` - `reverse_order` is `false` - `CharsToIgnore` includes `-` - Input string is `1234-5678-9012-3456` The resulting de-identified string is `****-****-****-3456`. Cloud DLP masks all but the last four characters. If `reverse_order` is `true`, all but the first four characters are masked as `1234-****-****-****`.
---@field reverseOrder? boolean Mask characters in reverse order. For example, if `masking_character` is `0`, `number_to_mask` is `14`, and `reverse_order` is `false`, then the input string `1234-5678-9012-3456` is masked as `00000000000000-3456`. If `masking_character` is `*`, `number_to_mask` is `3`, and `reverse_order` is `true`, then the string `12345` is masked as `12***`.

---Characters to skip when doing deidentification of a value. These will be left alone and skipped.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CharsToIgnore
---@field commonCharactersToIgnore? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CharsToIgnoreCommonCharactersToIgnoreEnum|string Common characters to not transform when masking. Useful to avoid removing punctuation.
---@field charactersToSkip? string Characters to not transform when masking.

---@alias gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CharsToIgnoreCommonCharactersToIgnoreEnum "COMMON_CHARS_TO_IGNORE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NUMERIC"|"ALPHA_UPPER_CASE"|"ALPHA_LOWER_CASE"|"PUNCTUATION"|"WHITESPACE"

---@alias gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CharsToIgnoreList gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CharsToIgnore[]

---Target used to match against for discovery with Cloud SQL tables.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CloudSqlDiscoveryTarget
---@field conditions? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2DiscoveryCloudSqlConditions In addition to matching the filter, these conditions must be true before a profile is generated.
---@field filter? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2DiscoveryCloudSqlFilter Required. The tables the discovery cadence applies to. The first target with a matching filter will be the one to apply to a table.
---@field generationCadence? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2DiscoveryCloudSqlGenerationCadence How often and when to update profiles. New tables that match both the filter and conditions are scanned as quickly as possible depending on system capacity.
---@field disabled? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2Disabled Disable profiling for database resources that match this filter.

---Use IAM authentication to connect. This requires the Cloud SQL IAM feature to be enabled on the instance, which is not the default for Cloud SQL. See https://docs.cloud.google.com/sql/docs/postgres/authentication and https://docs.cloud.google.com/sql/docs/mysql/authentication.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CloudSqlIamCredential

---Cloud SQL connection properties.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CloudSqlProperties
---@field cloudSqlIam? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CloudSqlIamCredential Built-in IAM authentication (must be configured in Cloud SQL).
---@field usernamePassword? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2SecretManagerCredential A username and password stored in Secret Manager.
---@field connectionName? string Optional. Immutable. The Cloud SQL instance for which the connection is defined. Only one connection per instance is allowed. This can only be set at creation time, and cannot be updated. It is an error to use a connection_name from different project or region than the one that holds the connection. For example, a Connection resource for Cloud SQL connection_name `project-id:us-central1:sql-instance` must be created under the parent `projects/project-id/locations/us-central1`
---@field maxConnections? number Required. The DLP API will limit its connections to max_connections. Must be 2 or greater.
---@field databaseEngine? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CloudSqlPropertiesDatabaseEngineEnum|string Required. The database engine used by the Cloud SQL instance that this connection configures.

---@alias gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CloudSqlPropertiesDatabaseEngineEnum "DATABASE_ENGINE_UNKNOWN"|"DATABASE_ENGINE_MYSQL"|"DATABASE_ENGINE_POSTGRES"

---Target used to match against for discovery with Cloud Storage buckets.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CloudStorageDiscoveryTarget
---@field conditions? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2DiscoveryFileStoreConditions Optional. In addition to matching the filter, these conditions must be true before a profile is generated.
---@field filter? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2DiscoveryCloudStorageFilter Required. The buckets the generation_cadence applies to. The first target with a matching filter will be the one to apply to a bucket.
---@field generationCadence? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2DiscoveryCloudStorageGenerationCadence Optional. How often and when to update profiles. New buckets that match both the filter and conditions are scanned as quickly as possible depending on system capacity.
---@field disabled? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2Disabled Optional. Disable profiling for buckets that match this filter.

---Message representing a set of files in Cloud Storage.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CloudStorageFileSet
---@field url? string The url, in the format `gs:///`. Trailing wildcard in the path is allowed.

---Options defining a file or a set of files within a Cloud Storage bucket.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CloudStorageOptions
---@field bytesLimitPerFile? string Max number of bytes to scan from a file. If a scanned file's size is bigger than this value then the rest of the bytes are omitted. Only one of `bytes_limit_per_file` and `bytes_limit_per_file_percent` can be specified. This field can't be set if de-identification is requested. For certain file types, setting this field has no effect. For more information, see [Limits on bytes scanned per file](https://docs.cloud.google.com/sensitive-data-protection/docs/supported-file-types#max-byte-size-per-file).
---@field filesLimitPercent? number Limits the number of files to scan to this percentage of the input FileSet. Number of files scanned is rounded down. Must be between 0 and 100, inclusively. Both 0 and 100 means no limit. Defaults to 0.
---@field fileSet? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2FileSet The set of one or more files to scan.
---@field bytesLimitPerFilePercent? number Max percentage of bytes to scan from a file. The rest are omitted. The number of bytes scanned is rounded down. Must be between 0 and 100, inclusively. Both 0 and 100 means no limit. Defaults to 0. Only one of bytes_limit_per_file and bytes_limit_per_file_percent can be specified. This field can't be set if de-identification is requested. For certain file types, setting this field has no effect. For more information, see [Limits on bytes scanned per file](https://docs.cloud.google.com/sensitive-data-protection/docs/supported-file-types#max-byte-size-per-file).
---@field sampleMethod? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CloudStorageOptionsSampleMethodEnum|string How to sample the data.
---@field fileTypes? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CloudStorageOptionsFileTypesItemEnumList List of file type groups to include in the scan. If empty, all files are scanned and available data format processors are applied. In addition, the binary content of the selected files is always scanned as well. Images are scanned only as binary if the specified region does not support image inspection and no file_types were specified. Image inspection is restricted to 'global', 'us', 'asia', and 'europe'.

---@alias gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CloudStorageOptionsFileTypesItemEnum "FILE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"BINARY_FILE"|"TEXT_FILE"|"IMAGE"|"WORD"|"PDF"|"AVRO"|"CSV"|"TSV"|"POWERPOINT"|"EXCEL"

---@alias gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CloudStorageOptionsFileTypesItemEnumList (gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CloudStorageOptionsFileTypesItemEnum|string)[]

---@alias gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CloudStorageOptionsSampleMethodEnum "SAMPLE_METHOD_UNSPECIFIED"|"TOP"|"RANDOM_START"

---Message representing a single file or path in Cloud Storage.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CloudStoragePath
---@field path? string A URL representing a file or path (no wildcards) in Cloud Storage. Example: `gs://[BUCKET_NAME]/dictionary.txt`

---A pattern to match against one or more file stores. At least one pattern must be specified. Regular expressions use RE2 [syntax](https://github.com/google/re2/wiki/Syntax); a guide can be found under the google/re2 repository on GitHub.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CloudStorageRegex
---@field bucketNameRegex? string Optional. Regex to test the bucket name against. If empty, all buckets match. Example: "marketing2021" or "(marketing)\d{4}" will both match the bucket gs://marketing2021
---@field projectIdRegex? string Optional. For organizations, if unset, will match all projects.

---Message representing a set of files in a Cloud Storage bucket. Regular expressions are used to allow fine-grained control over which files in the bucket to include. Included files are those that match at least one item in `include_regex` and do not match any items in `exclude_regex`. Note that a file that matches items from both lists will _not_ be included. For a match to occur, the entire file path (i.e., everything in the url after the bucket name) must match the regular expression. For example, given the input `{bucket_name: "mybucket", include_regex: ["directory1/.*"], exclude_regex: ["directory1/excluded.*"]}`: * `gs://mybucket/directory1/myfile` will be included * `gs://mybucket/directory1/directory2/myfile` will be included (`.*` matches across `/`) * `gs://mybucket/directory0/directory1/myfile` will _not_ be included (the full path doesn't match any items in `include_regex`) * `gs://mybucket/directory1/excludedfile` will _not_ be included (the path matches an item in `exclude_regex`) If `include_regex` is left empty, it will match all files by default (this is equivalent to setting `include_regex: [".*"]`). Some other common use cases: * `{bucket_name: "mybucket", exclude_regex: [".*\.pdf"]}` will include all files in `mybucket` except for .pdf files * `{bucket_name: "mybucket", include_regex: ["directory/[^/]+"]}` will include all files directly under `gs://mybucket/directory/`, without matching across `/`
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CloudStorageRegexFileSet
---@field excludeRegex? gcp.dlp_v2.StringList A list of regular expressions matching file paths to exclude. All files in the bucket that match at least one of these regular expressions will be excluded from the scan. Regular expressions use RE2 [syntax](https://github.com/google/re2/wiki/Syntax); a guide can be found under the google/re2 repository on GitHub.
---@field bucketName? string The name of a Cloud Storage bucket. Required.
---@field includeRegex? gcp.dlp_v2.StringList A list of regular expressions matching file paths to include. All files in the bucket that match at least one of these regular expressions will be included in the set of files, except for those that also match an item in `exclude_regex`. Leaving this field empty will match all files by default (this is equivalent to including `.*` in the list). Regular expressions use RE2 [syntax](https://github.com/google/re2/wiki/Syntax); a guide can be found under the google/re2 repository on GitHub.

---Identifies a single Cloud Storage bucket.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2CloudStorageResourceReference
---@field bucketName? string Required. The bucket to scan.
---@field projectId? string Required. If within a project-level config, then this must match the config's project id.

