---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2InspectResult
---@field findings? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2FindingList List of findings for an item.
---@field findingsTruncated? boolean If true, then this item might have more findings than were returned, and the findings returned are an arbitrary subset of all findings. The findings list might be truncated because the input items were too large, or because the server reached the maximum amount of resources allowed for a single API call. For best results, divide the input into smaller batches.

---The inspectTemplate contains a configuration (set of types of sensitive data to be detected) to be used anywhere you otherwise would normally specify InspectConfig. See https://docs.cloud.google.com/sensitive-data-protection/docs/concepts-templates to learn more.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2InspectTemplate
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The last update timestamp of an inspectTemplate.
---@field inspectConfig? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2InspectConfig The core content of the template. Configuration of the scanning process.
---@field displayName? string Display name (max 256 chars).
---@field description? string Short description (max 256 chars).
---@field allowLimitedAvailabilityInfoTypes? boolean Optional. Enables the use of [limited-availability built-in infoTypes](https://docs.cloud.google.com/sensitive-data-protection/docs/infotypes-reference#limited-availability-infotypes) in inspect_config. These infoTypes are supported only in specific regions and can cause scanning errors if used elsewhere.
---@field name? string Output only. The template name. The template will have one of the following formats: `projects/PROJECT_ID/inspectTemplates/TEMPLATE_ID` OR `organizations/ORGANIZATION_ID/inspectTemplates/TEMPLATE_ID`;
---@field createTime? string Output only. The creation timestamp of an inspectTemplate.

---@alias gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2InspectTemplateList gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2InspectTemplate[]

