---Summary statistics of a custom dictionary.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2LargeCustomDictionaryStats
---@field approxNumPhrases? string Approximate number of distinct phrases in the dictionary.

---Skips the data without modifying it if the requested transformation would cause an error. For example, if a `DateShift` transformation were applied an an IP address, this mode would leave the IP address unchanged in the response.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2LeaveUntransformed

---Message for specifying an adjustment to the likelihood of a finding as part of a detection rule.
---@class gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2LikelihoodAdjustment
---@field fixedLikelihood? gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2LikelihoodAdjustmentFixedLikelihoodEnum|string Set the likelihood of a finding to a fixed value.
---@field relativeLikelihood? number Increase or decrease the likelihood by the specified number of levels. For example, if a finding would be `POSSIBLE` without the detection rule and `relative_likelihood` is 1, then it is upgraded to `LIKELY`, while a value of -1 would downgrade it to `UNLIKELY`. Likelihood may never drop below `VERY_UNLIKELY` or exceed `VERY_LIKELY`, so applying an adjustment of 1 followed by an adjustment of -1 when base likelihood is `VERY_LIKELY` will result in a final likelihood of `LIKELY`.

---@alias gcp.dlp_v2.GooglePrivacyDlpV2LikelihoodAdjustmentFixedLikelihoodEnum "LIKELIHOOD_UNSPECIFIED"|"VERY_UNLIKELY"|"UNLIKELY"|"POSSIBLE"|"LIKELY"|"VERY_LIKELY"

